<caml:Content xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#"><p>(a)<span class="EnSpace"/>It shall be unlawful for a person to recommend to a prospective trustor any person to serve as trustee with knowledge or having reason to believe that the proposed trustee is insolvent or is about to become insolvent.</p><p>For purposes of this section, “insolvent” means a person who has ceased to pay that person’s debts as they become due or whose liabilities exceed that person’s assets.</p><p>(b)<span class="EnSpace"/>The provisions of this section shall not apply to any trustee named in any deed of trust or mortgage which secures a
				note or evidence of indebtedness on real property when such trustee acts solely in that capacity.</p></caml:Content>